-- title:
--   Regularity of g dj at smooth special-fibre points of the j⁻¹-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume $j$, in the shape of the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqModC ℚ`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15), lies in the $q$-expansion function field $F_{\top} =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model datum of type [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81). Write $F$ for the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (XHDRLevel.ΓM M H)` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ and $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. The hypotheses are: a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F$ characterised by $f_0 \in W_0$ iff $f_0 \cdot a' = a$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ for some power series $a,a'$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ with $a'$ nonzero modulo $p$; an element $\eta$ of $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $g \in W_0$ and $\eta = g \cdot D(j)$, where $j \in F$ is `XHDRLevel.jAt`; the condition that for every valuation subring $O$ of $F$ containing the image of $\mathbb{Q}$ there are $c,t \in O$ with $\eta = c \cdot D t$; a prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of the chart algebra `XHDRLevel.chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j^{-1}]$, such that the image of $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{p}$, the image of $\mathfrak{p}$ under the underlying map of the chart morphism `XHDRLevel.ιInf` lies in `𝔛.smoothLocus`, every $s \notin \mathfrak{p}$ has $s^{-1} \in W_0$, and the ideal generated by the image of $p$ in `Localization.AtPrime 𝔭.asIdeal` is prime. The conclusion: there exist $s \notin \mathfrak{p}$ in the chart algebra, natural numbers $n, k$ and families $a, b : \mathrm{Fin}\,k \to$ chart algebra with $s^{n} \cdot \eta = \sum_{i} a_i \cdot D(b_i)$ in $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the smooth-point regularity step for differentials on the Deligne–Rapoport model at $p$: a differential $g\,dj$ whose coefficient is integral for the Gauss valuation and which has no pole on the generic fibre admits, after inverting one function away from $\mathfrak{p}$, a presentation by chart-integral functions, i.e. is regular at the given smooth special-fibre point of the $j^{-1}$-chart. It is used in the construction extending $\omega_f$ over the model, in [`CuspForm.exists_forall_isRegularAt_of_not_mem_ssPlacesQExp_diffQExp_eq_intSeriesC_of_isIntegralQExp_residueField`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_forall_isRegularAt_of_not_mem_ssPlacesQExp_diffQExp_eq_intSeriesC_of_isIntegralQExp_residueField), en route to level lowering at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_exists_pow_smul_eq_sum_smul_D_chartAlgInf_of_mem_gauss_of_mem_smoothLocus.lean

